{"id": 31, "ts": 1780421365.696534, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I\u2019m inclined to align with Sarah\u2019s recommendation of **Candidate\u202fC**. The panel now has concrete evidence that C is *100\u202f% reliable* and consistently creates a positive crew atmosphere\u2014both essential for long\u2011distance operations where consistency and morale are critical. Moreover, C demonstrates strong decision\u2011making under pressure (quick, correct decisions and calmness in crises) and solid technical competence (understanding complicated technology).\nWhile Sarah notes C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas and an egocentric perception, the same source also emphasizes that these traits have not yet manifested in observable crew\u2011breakdowns; the candidate still fosters a constructive cockpit environment. Compared with the alternatives, B\u2019s pretentious tone and potential communication friction (as highlighted by Emily) could more directly erode crew cooperation, and D\u2019s hot temper and know\u2011it\u2011all attitude raise clear concerns for teamwork. A\u2019s leadership is shadowed by a show\u2011off reputation and resistance to new ideas, which may hinder adaptability on international routes.\nTherefore, despite the communication caveats, C\u2019s overall reliability, calmness, and decision quality make him the strongest fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
