{"id": 70, "ts": 1780421535.8940794, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s reliability and quick decision\u2011making, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the safer overall choice for a long\u2011distance pilot.\u202fB\u2019s very conscientious nature directly supports operational reliability, and his proven ability to handle stress\u202f\u2013\u202fcritical for the sustained pressures of international routes \u2013\u202fmatches the stress\u2011resilience criterion better than the limited evidence we have for C.\u202fAdditionally, B\u2019s strong weather\u2011assessment skill and excellent computer proficiency give him a clear technical and cognitive edge for complex, long\u2011haul flight planning.\nWhile Sarah notes that C \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere,\u201d the same notes also flag C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas, an egocentric style, and a lack of willingness to pursue further education. Those concerns raise serious doubts about crew cooperation and adaptability on extended missions where clear, collaborative communication and continuous learning are essential. In contrast, B\u2019s only reported communication issue is occasionally adopting the wrong tone, which is a more manageable behavior flaw than the broader interpersonal deficits observed for C.\nGiven B\u2019s balanced profile of reliability, stress resilience, and technical competence, I keep my vote for Candidate\u202fB."}
